{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/direction","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the arrow on the arpeggio sign, if present."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"direction","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","text":"MXLUpDown","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direction"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"direction","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUpDown","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV9directionAA9MXLUpDownOSgvp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"direction"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/direction"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/direction":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/direction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","text":"MXLUpDown"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/direction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the arrow on the arpeggio sign, if present."}],"title":"direction"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLUpDown":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlupdown","title":"MXLUpDown","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The up-down type is used for the direction of arrows and other pointed symbols like vertical accents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating which way the tip is pointing.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown"}}}